    /**
     * List every served version of a state session law, with HTTP metadata.
     *
     * <p>Every version of one STATE session law that we served or adopted, newest first, and which of them is current. The text of a law can be corrected after we first serve it (a better extraction of the same source, a re-collection), and the version you read yesterday is then not the one a plain call returns today. This route lists the versions with what identifies each (when we recorded it, its length, its hash, how the text was taken) and how its text can be read. It carries no text: read one version's text with <code>GET /us/session-laws/&#123;sessionLawId&#125;/body?version=N</code>. Charged: consumes credits.
     *
     * @param sessionLawId A STATE session law's id, for example <code>SSL_MN_2025S1_G_Y2025_C1</code>, from a <code>/us/session-laws/list</code> result.
     * @param options per-call overrides, or null
     * @return the parsed response and its HTTP metadata
     */
    public Response<SessionLawVersionsResponse> versionsWithResponse(String sessionLawId, RequestOptions options) {
        Transport.Call call = Transport.Call.of("GET", "/api/v1/us/session-laws/" + Paths.seg(sessionLawId) + "/versions").charged(true);
        return transport.execute(call, SessionLawVersionsResponse.class, options);
    }

